WEBVTT

NOTE
AI-generated narration. Synthetic demonstration data.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:12.110
Meet People O S, a working people operations system built by Alloyce Amos. It brings migration checks, support workflows, and human approvals into one connected workspace.

2
00:00:12.430 --> 00:00:24.040
Forty-eight fictional employees span thirteen countries. The directory, quality metrics, and country views all read from the same records, so the numbers stay connected as the data changes.

3
00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:33.787
In the migration hub, every exception has a clear explanation. You can compare the original value with the proposed correction and see the rule that raised it.

4
00:00:34.107 --> 00:00:46.367
Before an import, the migration lab parses the C S V and validates its fields. It reports missing values, duplicate identifiers, and invalid references without changing an employee record.

5
00:00:46.687 --> 00:00:55.883
The agent studio makes the work visible. Specialist tools extract the source, map its fields, check the records, and reconcile the proposed result.

6
00:00:56.203 --> 00:01:07.069
Each step has an inspectable output. These are real, deterministic checks. Optional A I helps explain the findings, while the decision to apply a change stays with the reviewer.

7
00:01:07.389 --> 00:01:17.142
After reviewing the proposal, approve the sixteen corrections. The sample records update, the open issues clear, and the data-quality measure reaches one hundred percent.

8
00:01:17.462 --> 00:01:28.561
The same approach extends to service requests. Teams review proposed assignments before they are applied. Onboarding and payroll readiness each have their own workflow and approval boundary.

9
00:01:28.881 --> 00:01:41.095
The people copilot answers in English or French, with visible references and optional browser voice. It can explain a migration or guide a new starter using clearly labeled example policies.

10
00:01:41.415 --> 00:01:51.214
Finally, the audit trail connects the decision to its result. Explore the live demo, inspect a workflow, or open the source to see the engineering behind the interface.
